    "show_share": true,
    "description": "AKU-ISMC Professor, Jonas Otterbeck, professor of Islamic Studies, has co-published a new article entitled  \"Music Version\" versus \"Vocals-Only\": Islamic Pop Music, Aesthetics, and Ethics  exploring the recent phenomena of pop-nashid. Looking at artists such as Maher Zain, Sami Yusuf and Harris J., the piece, co-written by musicologist Dr. Johannes Frandsen Skjelbo, analyses the historical development of different musical styles of pop-nashid, particularly the difference between 'vocals-only' and full instrumentation versions of the same songs.",
